One note about toString()

Even though you have two objects (e1 and e2), there is only one toString() method in the class. When 
you call System.out.println(e1), Java invokes that method with this referring to e1. When you call 
System.out.println(e2), Java invokes the same method, but this time this refers to e2. That's why the 
output reflects each object's own data even though the method implementation is shared.



