Q: Explain Encapsulation with a real-time example.
Answer

Consider a Bank Account. The account balance is private, so no one can modify it directly. 
The bank provides methods like deposit(), withdraw(), and getBalance(). These methods validate 
transactions before updating the balance. This protects the data and allows only valid operations, 
which is a real-world example of encapsulation.

